					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-10-19T07:19:15.017892+11:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-10-19T07:19:15.017892+11:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "gHrB529oQVCV1oJ/mHE+KQ=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## Lifecycle verification and one-time completed backlog cleanup\nCurrent SuperGame.image, Pharo13.1.0SNAPSHOT. Final run: BVCFairyCodexExamples 8, BVCFairyExamples 38, BVCFairyWindowTitleExamples 4: 50 successes, zero failures/errors/skips. An earlier test-double setup error (nonexistent ZnResponse class>>notFound) was corrected and the complete suite rerun. Focused examples cover success/body/result identity, network/body-read/parse/missing-terminal/history failure, 401 refresh/retry with each attempt closed, non-401 propagation, process termination unwind, slot/history preservation and root/child installation. Controlled HTTP doubles do not prove native TLS/network failure behavior.\n\n{{gtMethod:BVCFairyCodexExamples>>#repeatedNativeSocketResources}} performs ten real native TCP socket allocations without network connections/model calls, checks the exact three semaphore identities registered, executes controlled post with real Zinc client/stream close, checks handles nil and identities absent, and verifies zero registration growth each iteration. Native resource evidence: {{gtObject:id=876vdn2i18yl9kbqd34h0icyi}}. This is native allocation/release evidence, not a real TLS round trip.\n\nApproved one-time backlog selection was confined to the current shared Barry Codex history, nonnil parsed results, ZnStreamingEntity -> ZnChunkedReadStream with stored atEnd == true -> ZdcSecureSocketStream, nonnil socket handle, identity-deduplicated sockets. No atEnd messages/read/network probes, global socket sweep, GC or limit changes. Underlying secure streams were closed after rechecking eligibility. 337 selected/closed, 337 handles cleared; exactly 1011 selected semaphore identities went from registered to absent; global nonnil external registrations 1041 -> 30; zero cleanup errors. History 367 -> 368 during the cleanup interval because the chat continued naturally; no history entry/result/metadata was removed. Selection and native identity evidence: {{gtObject:id=7xculpl4mj77rgkxmjkfp4v2h}}; cleanup result: {{gtObject:id=6yra6yzchgu7fmaqh3u2daaqn}}. The old client remained active during implementation before migration; this selection is not a claim that no additional pre-installation completions exist.\n\nLive migration evidence: {{gtObject:id=c61wjqlks07j4fz2xeqj5kbjb}} (three Barry roots; their model consumers 1, 1 and 12; old-client model consumers zero, shared histories identical). Naturally occurring post-installation records were passively observed as materialized bodies with parsed results; external registrations remained 60 across observations separated by further natural completions: {{gtObject:id=63c4cd4y0st8xniwrnpbqz1va}} and {{gtObject:id=bzft82grv1lkhfudnh8q3imzn}}. This is bounded observation, not long-run proof. In-flight/pre-installation residual completions were not swept.\n\nRead-only Iceberg diff against CatalystDevKit reference commit inspected: only BV-Catalyst-Fairy-Core changes for BVCFairyChat, BVCFairyCodexClient and its four example/double classes; selector manifest {{gtObject:id=5iwlx4hivbq3waqpqlcemovjb}}. Upstream Codex and Zinc close source re-inspected unchanged. Pending source changes remain in the image; no source save/export, commit/push, BVC build, startup change, GemStone check or external checkout operation. Parent review is required before declaring completion; immediate cooperative-cancel interruption and native TLS failure-path execution remain unverified."
			}
		]
	},
